WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.630
Building Sentences.

2
00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:05.366
Day 2 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.116 --> 00:00:08.140
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:16.121
Today's goal: put words in the right order and make clear, correct sentences: positive, negative, and with am or is or are.

5
00:00:17.471 --> 00:00:18.325
Part 1.

6
00:00:18.605 --> 00:00:20.205
The basic English sentence.

7
00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:22.948
English has a fixed order.

8
00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.281
Most Indian languages put the verb at the end; English puts it second.

9
00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:29.997
Here is a quick table:

10
00:00:30.277 --> 00:00:33.349
Subject, and Verb, and Object, and Place, and Time.

11
00:00:33.629 --> 00:00:34.311
I.

12
00:00:34.591 --> 00:00:35.615
Verb: drink.

13
00:00:35.895 --> 00:00:37.069
Object: tea.

14
00:00:37.349 --> 00:00:38.799
Place: at the office.

15
00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:40.509
Time: every morning.

16
00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:41.493
Priya.

17
00:00:41.773 --> 00:00:42.903
Verb: fixed.

18
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:44.549
Object: the bug.

19
00:00:44.829 --> 00:00:46.514
Place: in the payment service.

20
00:00:46.794 --> 00:00:48.159
Time: yesterday.

21
00:00:48.439 --> 00:00:49.122
We.

22
00:00:49.402 --> 00:00:50.661
Verb: will deploy.

23
00:00:50.941 --> 00:00:52.370
Object: the update.

24
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.973
Place: to production.

25
00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.575
Time: on Friday.

26
00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:56.666
My son.

27
00:00:56.946 --> 00:00:58.055
Verb: plays.

28
00:00:58.335 --> 00:00:59.679
Object: cricket.

29
00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.175
Place: in the park.

30
00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:02.757
Time: after school.

31
00:01:04.107 --> 00:01:04.747
Tip:

32
00:01:05.027 --> 00:01:06.691
Hindi versus English order.

33
00:01:06.971 --> 00:01:07.696
Hindi:

34
00:01:07.976 --> 00:01:11.581
Main roz subah chai peeta hoon (I every morning tea drink).

35
00:01:11.861 --> 00:01:12.651
English:

36
00:01:12.931 --> 00:01:14.552
I drink tea every morning.

37
00:01:14.832 --> 00:01:16.816
Subject, then verb, then the rest.

38
00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.619
Part 2. am or is or are (the verb be).

39
00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:23.235
Here is a quick table:

40
00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.499
Subject, and be, and Example.

41
00:01:25.779 --> 00:01:27.037
I. be: am.

42
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:28.192
Example:

43
00:01:28.472 --> 00:01:30.947
I am a developer. then I'm a developer.

44
00:01:31.227 --> 00:01:34.277
He or She or It or one person. be: is.

45
00:01:34.557 --> 00:01:35.432
Example:

46
00:01:35.712 --> 00:01:37.717
She is at home. then She's at home.

47
00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.515
You or We or They or many. be: are.

48
00:01:40.795 --> 00:01:41.669
Example:

49
00:01:41.949 --> 00:01:43.656
They are late. then They're late.

50
00:01:45.006 --> 00:01:53.411
Use be for: who or what (I'm an engineer), where (He's in the meeting), how (We're tired), age (She's 28), and descriptions (The app is slow).

51
00:01:54.761 --> 00:01:55.508
Warning:

52
00:01:55.788 --> 00:01:56.855
Common mistake.

53
00:01:57.135 --> 00:02:00.207
I am work in Infosys. then I work at Infosys.

54
00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.729
(Don't use am with another action verb in the simple present.).

55
00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:05.975
Part 3.

56
00:02:06.255 --> 00:02:07.621
Negative sentences.

57
00:02:08.871 --> 00:02:10.236
Here is a quick table:

58
00:02:10.516 --> 00:02:12.969
Type, and Positive, and Negative. be.

59
00:02:13.249 --> 00:02:14.167
Positive:

60
00:02:14.447 --> 00:02:15.599
The server is up.

61
00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:16.775
Negative:

62
00:02:17.055 --> 00:02:19.487
The server isn't (is not) up. be (I).

63
00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:20.684
Positive:

64
00:02:20.964 --> 00:02:21.967
I am ready.

65
00:02:22.247 --> 00:02:23.143
Negative:

66
00:02:23.423 --> 00:02:24.425
I'm not ready.

67
00:02:24.705 --> 00:02:27.052
Action verb (I or you or we or they).

68
00:02:27.332 --> 00:02:28.249
Positive:

69
00:02:28.529 --> 00:02:29.596
I like coffee.

70
00:02:29.876 --> 00:02:30.772
Negative:

71
00:02:31.052 --> 00:02:32.268
I don't like coffee.

72
00:02:32.548 --> 00:02:34.553
Action verb (he or she or it).

73
00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:35.751
Positive:

74
00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:37.289
He works on weekends.

75
00:02:37.569 --> 00:02:38.465
Negative:

76
00:02:38.745 --> 00:02:40.217
He doesn't work on weekends.

77
00:02:40.497 --> 00:02:41.244
Past.

78
00:02:41.524 --> 00:02:42.441
Positive:

79
00:02:42.721 --> 00:02:43.937
We finished the task.

80
00:02:44.217 --> 00:02:45.113
Negative:

81
00:02:45.393 --> 00:02:47.399
We didn't finish the task. can.

82
00:02:47.679 --> 00:02:48.596
Positive:

83
00:02:48.876 --> 00:02:49.772
I can come.

84
00:02:50.052 --> 00:02:50.948
Negative:

85
00:02:51.228 --> 00:02:52.209
I can't come.

86
00:02:53.559 --> 00:02:56.994
After doesn't or didn't, the verb goes back to its base form:

87
00:02:57.274 --> 00:02:59.237
He doesn't works, then He doesn't work.

88
00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:01.504
Part 4.

89
00:03:01.784 --> 00:03:03.917
Make sentences longer (and clearer).

90
00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:08.687
Add details in the order: what, then where, then when, then why.

91
00:03:08.967 --> 00:03:10.098
I called the bank.

92
00:03:10.378 --> 00:03:11.957
I called the bank this morning.

93
00:03:12.237 --> 00:03:14.861
I called the bank this morning about my blocked card.

94
00:03:15.141 --> 00:03:19.557
I called the bank this morning about my blocked card, because I couldn't pay at the shop.

95
00:03:20.907 --> 00:03:21.867
Part 5.

96
00:03:22.147 --> 00:03:24.067
Conversation: at the reception.

97
00:03:25.317 --> 00:03:27.343
Here is how the conversation goes.

98
00:03:27.623 --> 00:03:29.031
Good morning.

99
00:03:29.311 --> 00:03:30.570
How can I help you?

100
00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:31.938
Good morning.

101
00:03:32.218 --> 00:03:33.882
I'm here for an interview.

102
00:03:34.162 --> 00:03:36.103
My name is Ashish Gupta.

103
00:03:36.383 --> 00:03:37.450
Welcome.

104
00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:38.946
Who are you meeting?

105
00:03:39.226 --> 00:03:40.698
I'm meeting Ms.

106
00:03:40.978 --> 00:03:42.834
Rao from the engineering team.

107
00:03:43.114 --> 00:03:45.119
The interview is at 10:30.

108
00:03:45.399 --> 00:03:46.509
Okay.

109
00:03:46.789 --> 00:03:48.453
She's in a meeting right now.

110
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:50.311
Can you wait for ten minutes?

111
00:03:51.661 --> 00:03:53.261
The conversation continues.

112
00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:55.056
Sure, no problem.

113
00:03:55.336 --> 00:03:57.213
Is there a washroom nearby?

114
00:03:57.493 --> 00:03:59.648
Yes, it's down the corridor, on the left.

115
00:03:59.928 --> 00:04:00.867
Thank you.

116
00:04:01.147 --> 00:04:02.363
I'll wait here.

117
00:04:03.713 --> 00:04:04.651
Part 6.

118
00:04:04.931 --> 00:04:05.849
Practice.

119
00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:07.739
1.

